---
/*
 * The Privacy Policy, in English (the default; store reviewers read it).
 * Every statement matches the app at release: the code as read on 2026-11-16,
 * plus the fixes in src/site.ts → APP, without which the build stops.
 * Evidence and plan: docs/GIZLILIK-INCELEMESI.md. Turkish: /tr/gizlilik.
 */
import Legal from "../layouts/Legal.astro";
import Ctl from "../components/Ctl.astro";
import Todo from "../components/Todo.astro";
import Providers from "../components/Providers.astro";
import Kept from "../components/Kept.astro";
import { DECISIONS } from "../site";
import { href, country } from "../i18n";
const lang = "en" as const;
const toc: [string, string][] = [
  ["summary", "Summary"], ["who", "Who we are"], ["device", "On the device"], ["connect", "When the app connects"],
  ["account", "Parent account"], ["not", "What we don't collect"], ["use", "How we use data"], ["share", "Who we share it with"],
  ["keep", "How long we keep it"], ["security", "Security"], ["children", "Children"], ["rights", "Your choices and rights"],
  ["site", "This website"], ["changes", "Changes"], ["contact", "Contact"],
];
---
<Legal lang={lang} page="privacy" title="Privacy Policy" eyebrow="Privacy"
  description="What the GlotKids app and website collect, when, where it goes and why; what they never ask for; and how to use your rights."
  intro="GlotKids is an app for children aged 4–8. It is built to work with as little data as possible. This policy describes what happens without an account and what changes when a parent opens one."
  toc={toc}>

  <div class="summary" id="summary">
    <h2>Summary</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><b>No ads, no analytics.</b> The app has no advertising, advertising ID, third-party analytics or crash-reporting tools, and does not track anyone.</li>
      <li><b>Without an account, your child's progress stays on the device.</b> We do not receive it.</li>
      <li><b>The app uses the internet</b> to download new worlds and updates. This sends technical data such as the IP address (see "When the app connects").</li>
      <li><b>A parent account is optional.</b> If you open one, a copy of your child's progress is kept with your account so you can continue on another device.</li>
      <li><b>We never ask children for personal information</b> — no name, birth date, photo, voice or location — and the app asks for no microphone, camera or location permission.</li>
      <li><b>We do not sell data or share it for advertising.</b></li>
    </ul>
  </div>

  <h2 id="who">Who we are</h2>
  <p>The data controller is <Ctl k="legalName" lang={lang} />, <Ctl k="address" lang={lang} />. Privacy contact: <Ctl k="privacyEmail" lang={lang} link />.</p>
  <p>The app is offered in: {DECISIONS.markets ? DECISIONS.markets.map((c) => country(c, lang)).join(", ") : <Todo lang={lang}>countries</Todo>}. For users in Türkiye, our notice under the Turkish data protection law (KVKK) is available in Turkish: <a href={href("kvkk", lang)} hreflang="tr">KVKK Aydınlatma Metni</a>.</p>

  <h2 id="device">1. On the device (no account needed)</h2>
  <p>So that your child can continue where they left off, the app keeps a small progress file in its own storage on the device:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>a random profile ID created by the app, and a label such as "1" or "2";</li>
    <li>the words met, how often and when;</li>
    <li>the games and worlds finished, and the place on the map;</li>
    <li>downloaded content (pictures, sounds, game data);</li>
    <li>for the parent's area: which game was played and when, and for each question answered whether the first choice was right and whether help was used.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>The parent's area, behind the parental gate, summarises these records on the device. The game records stay on the device even with a parent account: they are not part of the account backup. Without an account the progress file is <b>not sent to us</b> either. The profile ID is not a name, but it is still information about your child's use of the app, and we treat it that way. If your device's own backups (iCloud, Google) are on, the file may be included in them; Apple or Google keep those backups, and we cannot see them.</p>
  <p>The app also reads the device's volume level, because every question is spoken: if it is too low, the game waits. The volume level is used on the device only and is never stored or sent.</p>

  <h2 id="connect">2. When the app connects to the internet</h2>
  <p>The first worlds come with the app; later worlds are downloaded as your child moves on. When the device is online, the app:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>asks <b>our server</b> for new content and downloads it. Our server receives the IP address, the time, and the request itself (including the app version), and keeps these in its logs for security;</li>
    <li>asks <b>our app-update service</b> whether there is an update. That service receives the IP address, a random identifier created for this installation (it changes if the app is reinstalled), the operating system and the app version.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>Without an account, we do not link this data to a name or an email address, and we do not use it to build profiles.</p>

  <h2 id="account">3. With a parent account</h2>
  <p>The account is optional and belongs to the parent; no account is opened for the child. It is opened behind the parental gate, with an email code, Google or Apple. Before the account is created, the app tells you what will be backed up.</p>
  <ul>
    <li><b>Account data:</b> email address, account ID, sign-in method, and when the account was created and last used. With Apple you can choose "Hide My Email"; then we receive Apple's relay address.</li>
    <li><b>Progress backup:</b> a copy of the progress file described above, linked to your account, with its version, its last update time and the operating system (iOS or Android) of the device that last wrote it.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>When you sign in, and shortly after progress is saved, the device and your account are merged so every device signed in to the account has the same progress. The backup does not contain your child's name or birth date, but because it is linked to your account, we treat it as information about your child.</p>
  <p>Our authorised staff can see an account's email address and a summary of its backup (for example, how many words were met) in order to give support and handle requests. Every account action they take is recorded.</p>

  <h2 id="not">What we don't collect</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>A child's name, surname, birth date, school, photos, videos or voice recordings.</li>
    <li>Microphone, camera, photo library, contacts, calendar or location access.</li>
    <li>Advertising IDs, third-party analytics, crash reporting or tracking.</li>
    <li>Chat, messaging, sharing or contact with other users. No push notifications.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2 id="use">How we use data</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>To run the app and deliver content and updates (IP address, request data, installation identifier).</li>
    <li>To keep the service secure and fix problems (server logs).</li>
    <li>To provide the optional parent account and its backup (account data, progress backup).</li>
    <li>To answer your requests and support messages, and to show that deletions were carried out.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>We never use data for advertising, profiling or sale. For users in Türkiye, the legal bases under KVKK Article 5 are set out in the <a href={href("kvkk", lang)} hreflang="tr">KVKK notice</a>.{!DECISIONS.legalBasesReviewed && <> <Todo lang={lang}>legal bases to be confirmed by the lawyer</Todo></>}</p>

  <h2 id="share">Who we share it with</h2>
  <p>Only with the service providers below, only what each needs to provide its service, and with authorities when the law requires it.</p>
  <Providers lang={lang} />
  <p><b>Transfers outside Türkiye:</b> some of these providers are outside Türkiye. {DECISIONS.transfers ? DECISIONS.transfers[lang] : <Todo lang={lang}>the transfer mechanism in place for each provider (KVKK Art. 9)</Todo>}</p>

  <h2 id="keep">How long we keep it</h2>
  <div class="table-scroll"><table>
    <thead><tr><th>Data</th><th>Kept</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td>Progress on the device</td><td>Until the app is deleted or progress is reset ("Başa dön")</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Parent account and progress backup</td><td>Until you delete them. Accounts not used for a long time: <Kept k="inactiveAccount" lang={lang} /></td></tr>
      <tr><td>Record that an account was deleted (no email address)</td><td><Kept k="deletionRecord" lang={lang} /></td></tr>
      <tr><td>Server logs (IP address, request)</td><td><Kept k="serverLogs" lang={lang} /></td></tr>
      <tr><td>Sign-in provider's own records</td><td><Kept k="authProvider" lang={lang} /></td></tr>
      <tr><td>Our infrastructure backups</td><td><Kept k="infraBackups" lang={lang} />; data deleted from the live system is not brought back if a backup is restored</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Support emails</td><td><Kept k="supportMail" lang={lang} /></td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table></div>

  <h2 id="security">Security</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>All communication between the app and our services is encrypted (HTTPS).</li>
    <li>Every downloaded file is checked against its size and checksum before it is used.</li>
    <li>The sign-in session is kept in the device's secure storage.</li>
    <li>Only listed administrators can open our admin panel, and their account actions are recorded.</li>
    <li>Our infrastructure backups are encrypted.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>If you think you have found a security problem, please write to <Ctl k="privacyEmail" lang={lang} link />.</p>

  <h2 id="children">Children</h2>
  <p>GlotKids is made for children and does not ask them for personal information. Everything meant for adults — the account, downloads, resetting progress — is behind a parental gate. A parental gate is not legal parental consent, so only a parent or legal guardian may open an account. If we learn that a child has sent us personal information, we delete it.</p>

  <h2 id="rights">Your choices and rights</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><b>Delete the account:</b> in the app, tap "Ebeveyn" (Parent), answer the grown-up question, then "Hesabı sil" (Delete account). The account and the progress backup are deleted. Without the app: <a href={href("deletion", lang)}>Delete your account and data</a>.</li>
    <li><b>Delete only the backup</b> or <b>stop backing up:</b> on the same account screen; or sign out on every device.</li>
    <li><b>Reset progress:</b> "Başa dön" on the map (with a grown-up's confirmation) resets this device and, with an account, the backup too.</li>
    <li><b>Other requests</b> (access, correction, objection): email <Ctl k="privacyEmail" lang={lang} link />. We answer within 30 days, free of charge. Users in Türkiye may also apply under KVKK Article 11 and complain to the Personal Data Protection Board.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2 id="site">This website</h2>
  <p>This website is separate from the app. Its own code sets no cookies, stores nothing in your browser and contains no analytics or advertising; fonts, pictures and video are served from this site. The hosting provider keeps access logs (such as IP address and browser type) to deliver the site: {DECISIONS.webHosting ? DECISIONS.webHosting[lang] : <Todo lang={lang}>host, log period, and whether the host sets its own cookies</Todo>}.</p>

  <h2 id="changes">Changes</h2>
  <p>We update this policy when the app changes; the date and version are at the top. If what we collect, why, or who we share it with changes significantly, we tell you in the app and by email to account holders before the change. Where the law requires consent, we ask for it before the change applies.</p>

  <h2 id="contact">Contact</h2>
  <p>Privacy: <Ctl k="privacyEmail" lang={lang} link /> · Support: <Ctl k="supportEmail" lang={lang} link /> · Post: <Ctl k="address" lang={lang} /></p>
</Legal>
